    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite (the one `AcceptanceTest`) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the bulk-signup warning on the `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}` surface of this Spring Boot PetClinic app.\n\n**What the change does:** when more than 80 owners already carry today's registration date, responses include `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.\n\n**Edits:**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time).\n- `service/ClinicService.java` \u2014 declared `isBulkSignupDay()`.\n- `service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` \u2014 added a `BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD = 80` constant and `isBulkSignupDay()` returning `countRegisteredToday() > 80`. Extracted the existing \"owners registered today\" count into a shared `countRegisteredToday()` helper reused by the existing daily-capacity rule.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 marked `bulkSignupWarning` as an ignored MapStruct target (it's a global, derived-at-read flag, not an owner field).\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 set the flag from the service in both `getOwner` and `addOwner` responses.\n\nThe flag is evaluated against the current daily total on each read (mirroring the existing daily-limit rule's semantics), so the `GET`-based acceptance check sees the live value. `./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, all tests pass.\n\nNote: I left the existing 100/day daily-registration cap (`isDailyRegistrationAtCapacity`) unchanged \u2014 the new 80 threshold is a separate warning rule, consistent with the test comment describing them as distinct rules sharing the same accumulation path.",
